    class BaseEntity {
        +Integer id
    }
    class NamedEntity {
        +String name
    }
    class Person {
        +String firstName
        +String lastName
    }
    class Owner {
        +String address
        +String city
        +String telephone
        +List~Pet~ pets
    }
    class Pet {
        +String name
        +LocalDate birthDate
        +PetType type
        +List~Visit~ visits
    }
    class Visit {
        +LocalDate date
        +String description
    }
    class Vet {
        +Set~Specialty~ specialties
    }
    class PetType {
        +String name
    }
    class Specialty {
        +String name
    }

    BaseEntity <|-- NamedEntity
    BaseEntity <|-- Person
    NamedEntity <|-- PetType
    NamedEntity <|-- Specialty
    Person <|-- Owner
    Person <|-- Vet
    Owner "1" --> "0..*" Pet : owns
    Pet "1" --> "0..*" Visit : has
    Pet "*" --> "1" PetType : is of
    Vet "*" --> "*" Specialty : has
```

Every successful POST handler redirects rather than rendering a view directly:

```java
// PetController.processCreationForm
return "redirect:/owners/{ownerId}";
```

`RedirectAttributes.addFlashAttribute(...)` passes success messages across the redirect without polluting the URL. This prevents double-submission if the user presses the browser back button.

